  "description": "WUSZUJ crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C58 H69 Gd3 Mn4 N3 O28,3(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.037-3.951 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.88-129.89°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C58H69Gd3Mn4N3O28·3(CH3OH).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
